<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giorgio Vasari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511–<a href="/years/1574">1574</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giorgio Vasari was an Italian painter, architect and writer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arezzo">Arezzo</a> who worked for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. He designed the Uffizi offices from 1560 and the Vasari Corridor, and redecorated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-vecchio">Palazzo Vecchio</a>. His Lives of the Most Excellent Painters, Sculptors and Architects, first published in 1550, founded the discipline of art history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giorgio-vasari.jpg" alt="Giorgio Vasari" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Jacopo Zucchi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zucchi,_Jacopo_-_Vasari,_Giorgio_-_Uffizi_ICCD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
